bound-lock/1 about="The CLI and in-process Root host share the existing canonical unsigned lot admission judges and atomic result. The receiver chooses the admitted place, implementation, limits and injected canonical-line signer. Snapshot changes before commit refuse rather than rebase. Coverage is checked before acquiring signatures. Cancellation before visibility exposes no partial act; publication uncertainty and failures after commit retain the act identity for authenticated historical recovery without signing or reviving authority. A fresh repeated held lot needs no new signature. Public output is bounded data, not consumer console output." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=contract/native-root-admission value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="The CLI and in-process host share one contextual transaction. Receiver-selected persistence supplies CLI-compatible exclusion, authenticated results and heads, bounded inventory and atomic publication. Exact original declarations already carry their signatures; a bounded injected signer acquires receiver receipts. Root and receiver heads are checked before and after signing. Cancellation before visibility adds no partial act. Publication failure is uncertain until authenticated recovery by identity; recovery grants no current authorization." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=contract/contextual-transaction value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="The call was cancelled before the commit visibility point." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=class role=writes scope=refusal/host/cancelled value=operation
bound-lock/1 about="The contextual act fails a transaction precondition; nothing new is committed by that refusal." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=class role=writes scope=refusal/host/act value=operation
bound-lock/1 about="The coordinate of the observed host implementation digest in the native receipt set." at=policy:bound/receipts by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=audit/wire/receipt-instrument value=instrument/implementation
bound-lock/1 about="The declared snapshot cannot be decoded in its selected shape." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=class role=writes scope=refusal/host/snapshot-format value=input
bound-lock/1 about="The distribution carries native current receipts and the declared standing projection; the owning source retains full receipts and its signed ledger. The build-only publisher reuses the validated native fold, receipt renderer and byte sealer. Original TARGET, complete receipts and signed admission messages are exported byte for byte in an external publication-history@1 JSON document: records target/receipts/admitted with their existing SHA-256 digests. Its digest is named in receipts/history; identity does not confer current authority. Historical inspection needs those bytes and refuses missing or altered history. Existing transport response bytes bound the document. A clean public checkout verifies and reuses its projected receipts without a private memo or signing key." at=policy:receipt-publication by=target form=alphabet measure=id needs=transport/response-bytes role=writes scope=publish/receipt-history shape=sources/receipt-history value=current-with-history@1
bound-lock/1 about="The embedding host supplies the instrument name, implementation runtime, policy and snapshot per call. Import and admission neither interpret consumer argv nor write its console. Canonical-line signing remains separate from signature frames. Offered bytes cannot select authority, verification, instrument ports or larger receiver budgets." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=contract/native-call-context value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="The fixture instrument receives the publication projection of already admitted folded configuration; historical signatures are not copied as local authority." at=witness:content-verified-fold-work-reuse by=target form=alphabet measure=digest role=writes scope=uses/process-readings value=sha256:59e99441730bba52d90f5a97413b6507c215e2c4b0deaac8ad15e3ec3d295a6f
bound-lock/1 about="The fourteen proposed local-mirror source URLs were withdrawn after their draft inputs were removed. Selected standing and runtime digests remain unchanged. No matching public world delivery has been verified for those bytes; clean native closure remains unpaid. Public sources must deliver the exact selected bytes, or an explicit reviewed world release and re-pin is required; no newest-by-URL or local-store substitution." at=policy:bound/019-public-source-ci by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=rationale/019/public-source-delivery value=present
bound-lock/1 about="The historical authority prefix differs from the supplied Root history." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=class role=writes scope=refusal/host/historical-snapshot value=integrity
bound-lock/1 about="The host adapter parses literal JavaScript imports when identifying the implementation behind receipts. It executes no module and does not inventory domain exports, duplicates or literals. It does not enforce arbitrary dynamic-import closure or claim a capsule sandbox." at=policy:host-module-identity by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=rationale/host/module-parser value=present
bound-lock/1 about="The host call lacks valid receiver-selected context." at=policy:contextual-host by=target form=alphabet measure=class role=writes scope=refusal/host/context value=input
bound-lock/1 about="The native authenticated reference route opens separately signed carriers using externally declared host authority, forms and bounded transport; positive and named negative cases are measured by the selected publication world. A zero count is conditional on the identified fixed image and laid form content; it grants neither current-answer reuse nor final archive acceptance." at=policy:bound/020-public-api-coverage by=target form=interval measure=count needs=contract/published/authenticated-reference role=reads scope=contract/published/authenticated-reference value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="The native object route is measured through the selected publication world against a separately identified fixed instrument image and immutable formed places. The quartet binds the published contract, yes/no data and executable CLI vector; a zero count certifies that declared fixture condition only. Exact archive installation and another-machine portability are separate obligations." at=policy:bound/020-public-api-coverage by=target form=interval measure=count needs=contract/published/optional-wasm-adapter role=reads scope=contract/published/optional-wasm-adapter value=0..0
